# The Darkest Day over Wyndon: the sky gone red and the city holding its breath. Strings in D minor on a running
# ostinato, a low choir that rises bar by bar, timpani rolling underneath and a brass call that never resolves until
# the loop turns. The same by day and night: the Darkest Day has no hour.
# Original composition for this game (plan 33 · GL7), in the modern sound. Not wired yet: Wyndon's own song stands in
# under the red sky until the user has heard it (rulings, "After the Hall of Fame in Galar").
